{"type":"assistant_message","payload":{"text":"I read this as a new-tab click that never forwarded homepage/blank into `createBrowserTab` — that path is fixed and verified.\n\n**Root cause.** “New Browser Tab” called `onNewBrowser()` with no URL. App then did `createBrowserTab(url ?? \"http://localhost:3000\")`, so a configured homepage was ignored and a blank homepage never became `about:blank`. A cancelled worker had already started passing `newBrowserTabUrl()` from the popover; that change was kept.\n\n**Fix.** Popover still resolves homepage or `about:blank` at click. App now uses the same resolver for the menu callback and the shortcut, then hands that URL to the existing `createBrowserTab` flow.\n\n**Files.**\n- `ui/src/App.tsx`\n- `ui/src/App.test.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/NewTabPopover.tsx` (preserved)\n- `ui/src/components/NewTabPopover.test.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/TabBar.test.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/NewTabPopover.browserTab.runtime.test.tsx` (new)\n\n**Verification.**\n- Focused: NewTabPopover 10, runtime visible-tab 2, TabBar 13, browserSettings 7, BrowserPane 2, BrowserToolbar 6, browserLifecycle 1 — pass\n- App homepage + blank menu tests — pass\n- Playwright (Vite + Tauri stub): blank → tab `Browser` / `about:blank`; homepage → tab `Browser` / `https://example.com/start`\n\n**Not this change.**\n- `npm --prefix ui run build` fails on dirty `ui/src/state/workspaceStore.test.tsx` (`TS7016` missing `jsdom` types). Untouched.\n- Concurrent App.test “performance optimizations” cases fail on pre-existing `SettingsDialog` import / inline `onOpenSettings`. Untouched.\n\n**Review.** NewTabPopover still owns the menu; App only forwards the resolved URL. No new helpers, `any`, or logging. App.tsx remains oversized (pre-existing ~803 LOC); this change is an import plus two call sites.\n\nNo commit."}}
